<HelpTab>
    <HelpSection Title="On this device">
        <FluentText>
            Under <strong>This device</strong>, select <strong>Turn on notifications for this device</strong> and allow
            them when your browser or phone asks. Use <strong>Send a test</strong> to check they arrive. If they're
            blocked, allow notifications for Lanyard in your browser's site settings, then try again.
        </FluentText>
        <FluentText>
            <strong>Your devices</strong> lists everywhere notifications go. Remove any you no longer use.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Choosing what you get">
        <FluentText>
            Under <strong>What you get</strong>, choose <strong>Push</strong> and <strong>Email</strong> for each kind of
            notification. Push goes to every device under Your devices. Password, sign-in and invite emails
            always arrive.
        </FluentText>
        <FluentText>
            Turn off <strong>Show message text in notifications</strong> if others can see your lock screen. Chat
            notifications then only say who the message is from.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
